WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.540
A sensor sits in a small creek in Virginia.

2
00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:10.560
It checks the oxygen in the water every 15 minutes.

3
00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:16.300
On one summer day, the water held far more oxygen at 6 p.m.

4
00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:18.720
It held less in the early morning.

5
00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:22.140
Why does creek oxygen go up and down?

6
00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:26.940
And if plants make their own food, why do they use oxygen too?

7
00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:30.910
Look inside one green leaf cell.

8
00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:36.270
It has a chloroplast, a green part of the cell that takes in light.

9
00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.430
Here, photosynthesis happens.

10
00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:44.730
Photosynthesis uses radiant energy, such as light from the sun.

11
00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:48.890
It makes sugar, called glucose, and oxygen.

12
00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:52.130
Carbon dioxide and water go in.

13
00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:54.710
Sugar and oxygen come out.

14
00:00:55.483 --> 00:00:58.743
The same cell also has mitochondria.

15
00:00:59.443 --> 00:01:03.203
Mitochondria are found in almost all plant and animal cells.

16
00:01:04.143 --> 00:01:06.583
Most cellular respiration happens in them.

17
00:01:07.383 --> 00:01:09.763
Respiration joins sugar with oxygen.

18
00:01:10.483 --> 00:01:12.763
This releases energy the cell can use.

19
00:01:13.843 --> 00:01:17.643
Carbon dioxide and water come out, and some energy leaves as heat.

20
00:01:18.433 --> 00:01:22.093
A reactant is a substance that goes into a process.

21
00:01:22.773 --> 00:01:24.993
A product is a substance that comes out.

22
00:01:25.853 --> 00:01:29.633
The products of photosynthesis are the reactants of respiration.

23
00:01:30.473 --> 00:01:33.753
The products of respiration are the reactants of photosynthesis.

24
00:01:34.873 --> 00:01:38.313
Processes that depend on each other like this are interdependent.

25
00:01:39.013 --> 00:01:40.853
The same matter is used again.

26
00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:43.387
Energy moves differently.

27
00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:49.667
It flows one way. Light from the sun becomes chemical energy in sugar.

28
00:01:50.827 --> 00:01:53.507
Respiration releases that energy for the cell.

29
00:01:54.387 --> 00:01:55.847
Some of it leaves as heat.

30
00:01:56.827 --> 00:01:58.827
Energy changes form as it goes.

31
00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:01.770
Think of the creek as a tub.

32
00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:04.870
The tap is running, and the drain is open.

33
00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:07.490
Sunlight turns the tap on.

34
00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:11.250
The tap is photosynthesis, adding oxygen.

35
00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:13.350
The drain never closes.

36
00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:17.870
The drain is respiration, by nearly every living thing.

37
00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:22.910
By day, the tap often runs faster, so oxygen climbs.

38
00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:27.530
After dark, only the drain is open, so oxygen falls.

39
00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:33.730
Plants make new sugar only in light, but they respire day and night.
